  <h1>Privacy Policy for Socially</h1>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> November 9, 2026</p>

  <p>Socially is a desktop application designed to help
  authorized users manage and schedule content publishing
  to Facebook Pages and supported Meta platforms.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Information We Process</h2>
    <p>When authorized by a user, Socially may process
    Facebook account identifiers, Page identifiers,
    Page names, access tokens, publishing permissions,
    video content, captions, scheduling information,
    and publication results.</p>
    <p>Actual data processing depends on the features
    enabled and permissions granted.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>Socially processes authorized information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Connect accounts and managed Facebook Pages.</li>
      <li>Schedule and publish selected content.</li>
      <li>Monitor publishing status and errors.</li>
      <li>Manage authorized content workflows.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Data Storage and Security</h2>
    <p>Socially processes information required to
    operate its authorized publishing features.</p>
    <p><strong>Implementation details:</strong>
    Before publishing this policy, confirm and describe
    where credentials and other information are stored,
    whether they are encrypted, how long they are retained,
    and whether external services receive any data.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Third-Party Platforms</h2>
    <p>Socially integrates with Meta platforms,
    including Facebook, using authorized APIs.
    Information submitted to Meta is subject to
    Meta's applicable terms and privacy policies.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Data Sharing</h2>
    <p>Socially transfers information to Meta as
    necessary to perform authorized publishing operations.</p>
    <p><strong>Implementation details:</strong>
    Disclose any additional service providers or
    third-party data sharing used by the application.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
    <p>Users may request deletion of information
    maintained by Socially by contacting the email
    address below.</p>
    <p>Requests will be reviewed and handled in
    accordance with applicable legal and platform
    requirements. Users may also revoke Socially's
    Facebook permissions through their Facebook
    account settings.</p>
    <p>Email: YOUR_EMAIL_ADDRESS</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. User Choices</h2>
    <p>Users can stop using Socially and revoke
    connected Meta permissions. Requests concerning
    locally stored application data may be directed
    to the contact address below.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when Socially's
    features, data practices, or applicable
    requirements change.</p>
  </section>

